[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:On Strike]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.29]Who will be driving the buses next week? | 下周谁来驾驶公共汽车？
[00:15.18]Busmen have decided to go on strike next week. | 公共汽车司机决定下星期罢工。
[00:19.77]The strike is due to begin on Tuesday. | 罢工定于星期二开始。
[00:23.83]No one knows how long it will last. | 谁也不知道罢工会持续多久。
[00:27.51]The busmen have stated that the strike will continue until general agreement is reached about pay and working conditions. | 司机们声称此次罢工将一直持续到就工资和工作条件达成全面协议为止。
[00:38.37]Most people believe that the strike will last for at least a week. | 多数人认为罢工至少会持续一个星期。
[00:44.15]Many owners of private cars are going to offer 'free rides' to people on their way to work. | 很多私人车主打算为去上班的人们提供“免费搭乘”。
[00:52.07]This will relieve pressure on the trains to some extent. | 这将在某种程度上减轻对火车的压力。
[00:56.81]Meanwhile, a number of university students have volunteered to drive buses while the strike lasts. | 与此同时，有一部分大学生在罢工期间自愿驾驶公共汽车。
[01:05.56]All the students are expert drivers, | 所有的学生都是驾驶能手，
[01:08.88]but before they drive any of the buses, they will have to pass a special test. | 但在驾驶公共汽车之前，他们必须通过一项专门测验。
[01:16.72]The students are going to take the test in two days' time. | 学生们将在两天后参加测验。
[01:21.72]Even so, people are going to find it difficult to get to work. | 即便如此，人们仍会感到上班有困难。
[01:27.43]But so far, the public has expressed its gratitude to the students in lettters to the Press. | 但到目前为止，公众已经通过给报界的信件表达了对学生们的感激之情。
[01:35.31]Only one or two people have objected that the students will drive too fast! | 只有一两个人提出反对意见，说学生们会把车开得太快！
